@ November 24, 2026

Hello!

In the spirit of business as usual: here is another batch of security
advisories, bug fixes and feature improvements in internal and external
components.

Of note are reliability improvements in DHCP and PPP client handling which
showed good results in public calls for testing on the forum.  This update
also switches from Hyperscan use to Vectorscan, which is a drop-in change
and has some other portability benefits as well.

Monit was updated to 6.1.0 which may have more hidden incompatibilities.
Special thanks to Konstantinos Spartalis for a timely submission on fixing
these proactively.

PHP 8.5.13 and several FreeBSD security advisories are included as well.

We have been working a bit on discussing restructures for how we deal with
hotfix and patch releases in the future.  There is a plan going forward,
but we will field test it before saying much more.

Here are the full patch notes:

o system: add user API key descriptions
o system: throw read-only for clear log action
o system: separate dashboard widget init from slower start routine
o system: drop gateway threshold constraints that never ran (contributed by Stephen Cox)
o system: show the stored history range in the log viewer (contributed by Greelan)
o system: name the setting in backup provider validation messages (contributed by Greelan)
o system: fix Norwegian/Vietnamese not being translated
o system: fix argument reversal in str_starts_with() in getLandingPage()
o reporting: netflow: modify netgraph NAT accounting to prevent duplicate flow records
o interfaces: validate PPP array fields as well[1] (contributed by superbot-helper)
o interfaces: update MAC vendor mappings
o interfaces: protect against empty PPP iteration
o interfaces: remove newwanip even from DHCP alias handling
o interfaces: flatten the successful TIMEOUT branch of DHCP
o interfaces: introduce DAD sleep for 6to4 and 6RD trackers
o interfaces: remove the PPP uptime option
o interfaces: defer PPP to after rc.bootup completes
o interfaces: do not throw an error on getting stats for interfaces
o interfaces: use interfaces_merge_pending() in newwanip events when interface settings are being applied
o firewall: aliases: add Kosovo country code "XK" and remove unused "EU" workaround
o firewall: fix multiple issues in GIF, GRE, Bridge, LAGG and PPP (contributed by Stephen Cox)
o firewall: fix resolving source NAT target network (contributed by Steve Kerrison)
o firewall: replace firewall_rule_lookup.php with ruleLookupAction()
o firewall: fix multiple issues in aliases, groups and sessions (contributed by Stephen Cox)
o firewall: generate a fallback UUID when empty during export in migration assistant
o firewall: do not count the template rule of an empty list for DNatSequenceField (contributed by Stephen Cox)
o captive portal: partially revert the IPv4 roaming removal to keep dual stack working
o captive portal: make zone ID a text field and constrain it to be unique
o firmware: support patch syntax for initial releases
o firmware: make subscription and flavour use more strict[2] (reported by anhlvk48 from Apex Orion)
o intrusion detection: allow % in policy descriptions (contributed by Gennaro Cimmino)
o intrusion detection: also catch urllib3 exceptions in rule downloader
o intrusion detection: prevent negative values in priority field
o intrusion detection: pattern matcher "hs" is now provided by drop-in replacement Vectorscan (contributed by MajorP93)
o ipsec: check pre-shared key uniqueness when only the remote identifier changes (contributed by Stephen Cox)
o ipsec: better handling of "(unnamed)" connections in dashboard widget
o kea: waste less prefix space when calculating IA_NA and IA_PD
o kea: align domain registration of static reservations with ddns_qualifying_suffix instead of overloading DHCP options
o lang: added Vietnamese as a new language, which was actually shipped in 26.7.9 but did not yet work
o monit: fix faulty escape sequence in password write
o monit: update polltime mask to include slash character (contributed by electronicm)
o monit: allow DHCP interfaces in service settings (contributed by Konstantinos Spartalis)
o monit: fix 6.1 incompatibilities and substitute deprecations (contributed by Konstantinos Spartalis)
o unbound: remove support for deprecated blocklistproject entries (contributed by Konstantinos Spartalis)
o unbound: fix a misinterpretation of IPv6 addresses in blocklist handling (contributed by Stephen Cox)
o wireguard: add $enabled flag for support for toggleClientAction()
o wireguard: fix restart action without instance parameter (contributed by Konstantinos Spartalis)
o backend: restrict service stop and similar actions to "wheel,wwwonly" (contributed by Bill Flood)
o backend: pluginctl enforce primary mode as selected by caller (reported by Dominik Münsterer)
o shell: improve error handling of the restore backup functionality (contributed by Alok K. Dhir)
o shell: opnsense-version: add package tree hash support
o tests: add a test case for getNodeCotent()
o plugins: partial rollout of restricting service stop and similar actions to "wheel,wwwonly" (contributed by Greelan)
o plugins: os-caddy 2.2.4[3]
o plugins: os-ddclient 1.34[4]
o plugins: os-firewall-legacy 1.2[5]
o plugins: os-intrusion-detection-content-et-open 1.0.3 switch to suricata-8.0 ruleset and add new ET categories (contributed by juergen2025sys)
o plugins: os-zabbix-agent 1.20[6]
o plugins: os-zabbix-proxy 1.18[7]
o src: tzdata: import tzdata 2026f[8]
o src: vfs: avoid integer overflow when faulting[9]
o src: openssl: update to 3.5.9[10]
o src: openzfs: data corruption involving pending block frees[11]
o src: ktls: check the record type message holds its byte[12]
o src: linux: kernel memory disclosure via Linuxulator extattr syscalls[13]
o src: multiple vulnerabilities in the ocs_fc driver[14]
o src: netlink: local privilege escalation via netlink heap buffer overflow[15]
o src: gssd: do not map unrecognized Kerberos principals to UID 0[16]
o src: nfsd: remote code execution via stateid type confusion[17]
o src: vfs: privilege escalation via inotify watch descriptor wraparound[18]
o src: vfs: apsicum and O_RESOLVE_BENEATH bypass at mount roots[19]
o src: ipsec: stream cipher counter reuse[20]
o src: unix: privilege escalation via shutdown race on unix sockets[21]
o src: vmm: bhyve guests can panic the host on Intel CPUs[22]
o src: kqueue: multiple vulnerabilities in kevent[23]
o src: freebsd32: privilege escalation via compat32 recvmsg control messages[24]
o src: socket: privilege escalation via socket unsplice timeout[25]
o src: sound: privilege escalation via sound software buffer resizing[26]
o src: bsnmp: fix multiple vulnerabilities[27]
o src: vm: privilege escalation via prefaulting on largepage mappings[28]
o src: fdescfs: privilege escalation via missing access checks[29]
o src: vfs: directory permission bypass via open[30]
o src: tcp: local privilege escalation via TCP MSG_OOB handling[31]
o src: tmpfs: failed to clear set-group-ID bit on new files[32]
o ports: ca_root_nss 3.134[33]
o ports: kea 3.0.5[34]
o ports: monit 6.1.0[35]
o ports: nss 3.133[36]
o ports: php 8.5.13[37]
o ports: py-duckdb 2.0.0[38]
o ports: vectorscan 5.4.14[39]


Stay safe,
Your OPNsense team

--
